gers</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Synthesis of semantic modeling and risk analysis methodology applied to animal welfare</article-title><source>Animal</source><year>2008</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>1061</fpage><lpage>1072</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S1751731108002139</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Anonymous</collab></person-group><article-title>Scientists' assessment of the impact of housing and management on animal welfare</article-title><source>J Appl Animal Welfare Sci</source><year>2001</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1207/S15327604JAWS0401_2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bracke</surname><given-names>MBM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>RICHPIG: a semantic model to assess enrichment materials for pigs</article-title><source>Animal Welfare</source><year>2008</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>304</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bracke</surname><given-names>MBM</given-names></name><name><surname>Spruijt</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Metz</surname><given-names>JHM</given-names></name><name><surname>Schouten</surname><given-names>WGP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decision support system for overall welfare assessment in pregnant sows A: Model structure and weighting procedure</article-title><source>J Anim Sci</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>1819</fpage><lpage>1834</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12162649</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bracke</surname><given-names>MBM</given-na