se study and simulation results</article-title><source>Biometrics J</source><year>1996</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/bimj.4710380107</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>GenStat Committee</collab></person-group><source>The guide to GenStat</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Oxford, UK, VSN Int</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bekoff</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Townsend</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Rollin</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Animals in science: Some areas revisited</article-title><source>Anim Behav</source><year>1992</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>484</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0003-3472(92)90057-G</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dawkins</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Battery hens name their price: Consumer demand theory and the measurement of ethological 'needs'</article-title><source>Anim Behav</source><year>1983</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>1195</fpage><lpage>1205</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0003-3472(83)80026-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bracke</surname><given-names>MBM</given-names></name><name><surname>Spruijt</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Metz</surname><given-names>JHM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Overall welfare assessment reviewed. Part 1: Is it possible?</article-title><source>Netherl J Agric Sci</source><year>1999</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>279</fpage><lpage>291</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>